@startuml BastionSeguridadAccesos
' Diagrama especifico de bastion: seguridad y accesos

skinparam backgroundColor #FAFBFC
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundcorner 12
skinparam defaultFontName DejaVu Sans
skinparam ArrowThickness 1.3
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #FFF8DC
skinparam noteBorderColor #B38F00

skinparam rectangle {
  BackgroundColor #FFFFFF
  BorderColor #2E4053
  FontColor #1B2631
}

skinparam cloud {
  BackgroundColor #EAF2F8
  BorderColor #1F618D
  FontColor #154360
}

title Bastion mimas.net - Seguridad y Flujos de Acceso SSH

legend left
  == Bastion ==
  Hostname: bastion.mimas.net
  IP: 192.168.50.2 (red-admin)

  == Uso principal ==
  - Punto de salto (jump host) para acceso externo
  - Control de acceso por llave SSH
  - Enrutamiento administrado a segmentos internos
endlegend

cloud "Admin Externo\nLaptop/Operador" as external
node "Host KVM\nred-admin GW 192.168.50.1" as kvmhost
node "Bastion\nbastion.mimas.net\n192.168.50.2" as bastion #E8F8F5

package "Redes internas del laboratorio" {
  node "Apps\n192.168.20.0/24" as appnet
  node "DB/Redis\n192.168.30.0/24" as dbnet
  node "Principal\n192.168.10.0/24" as frontnet
  node "Storage\n192.168.40.0/24" as stnet
  node "Ceph Cluster\n192.168.60.0/24" as cephnet
}

rectangle "Controles de seguridad en Bastion" as controls #FCF3CF
note right of controls
  SSH:
  - PasswordAuthentication no
  - PermitRootLogin no
  - AllowTcpForwarding yes
  - AllowAgentForwarding yes

  Firewall (UFW):
  - deny incoming (default)
  - allow outgoing (default)
  - allow 22/tcp

  Operacion:
  - Acceso por llaves compartidas del proyecto
  - Jump host para ProxyJump (-J)
end note

external --> bastion : SSH 22 (llave)
external --> bastion : ssh -J user@192.168.50.2 user@<destino>

bastion --> kvmhost : Rutas estaticas via 192.168.50.1
kvmhost --> appnet : Forward/NAT controlado
kvmhost --> dbnet : Forward/NAT controlado
kvmhost --> frontnet : Forward/NAT controlado
kvmhost --> stnet : Forward/NAT controlado
kvmhost --> cephnet : Forward/NAT controlado

bastion ..> controls : Politicas activas

note bottom of external
  Escenario A (local lab):
  - El host con bridges puede entrar directo a nodos internos.

  Escenario B (externo):
  - El acceso se realiza via bastion.
end note

@enduml